1
00:00:05,757 --> 00:00:09,947
We carry two mistakes about
appearances, and they mirror each other.

2
00:00:10,766 --> 00:00:12,235
The first is familiar.

3
00:00:12,315 --> 00:00:17,262
We treat what we see and touch as if
each thing had a fixed nature of its own,

4
00:00:17,342 --> 00:00:19,790
simply there, waiting to be found.

5
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:24,463
This is the habit of reification,
and it rarely shows up as a view.

6
00:00:24,543 --> 00:00:27,552
It shows up as the plain
sense that things are real.

7
00:00:28,386 --> 00:00:30,766
The second is less often noticed.

8
00:00:30,846 --> 00:00:33,510
Having heard that things
lack a fixed nature,

9
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:36,540
we imagine they must be faint and ghostly,

10
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,891
like shadows we could brush aside.

11
00:00:38,971 --> 00:00:44,928
Both mistakes share one assumption: that
solidity and emptiness exclude each other.

12
00:00:45,017 --> 00:00:47,074
Four points loosen that assumption.

13
00:00:47,943 --> 00:00:50,010
First, mutual dependence.

14
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:52,646
Nothing is long or short in itself.

15
00:00:52,726 --> 00:00:56,450
A stick is long beside a
pebble, and short beside a tree.

16
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:59,770
A person is a parent only
because there is a child.

17
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:03,909
"My car" is its wheels,
its engine, the road,

18
00:01:03,989 --> 00:01:06,803
the driver's purpose,
and the name we give it.

19
00:01:06,883 --> 00:01:11,060
Gather those relations, and no
car is found lying underneath.

20
00:01:11,869 --> 00:01:14,411
Modern physics reaches a similar place.

21
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:17,984
In Carlo Rovelli's relational
reading of quantum theory,

22
00:01:18,064 --> 00:01:22,685
and in Karen Barad's account, relation
comes before the things related.

23
00:01:22,765 --> 00:01:27,414
Yet both still treat the relating as
a structure to be finally described:

24
00:01:27,494 --> 00:01:31,802
a ground. The Middle Way asks whether
that ground can be found at all.

25
00:01:31,882 --> 00:01:35,281
Relations are as empty as
the things they relate.

26
00:01:35,361 --> 00:01:40,253
So mutual dependence is not a hidden
structure tying everything together.

27
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:45,326
It is simply what is found when we look
for an essence and find only relations.

28
00:01:46,145 --> 00:01:48,374
Second, empty appearances.

29
00:01:48,454 --> 00:01:51,717
A coin pressed into the
palm feels hard and weighty.

30
00:01:51,797 --> 00:01:55,970
It has no essence of its own,
and it is not flimsy for that.

31
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:58,361
Emptiness is not harmlessness either.

32
00:01:58,441 --> 00:02:02,831
A car is empty in exactly this
sense, and when it strikes someone,

33
00:02:02,911 --> 00:02:05,317
the injury is entirely real.

34
00:02:05,397 --> 00:02:07,641
Emptiness does not dim appearance.

35
00:02:07,721 --> 00:02:11,282
It is the way appearance
is: vivid, usable,

36
00:02:11,362 --> 00:02:13,610
and empty, all at once.

37
00:02:14,461 --> 00:02:17,996
Third, functioning without
inherent existence.

38
00:02:18,076 --> 00:02:22,343
A bridge carries traffic, though
no single part of it is the bridge.

39
00:02:22,423 --> 00:02:27,099
Steel, deck, supports and the
name work together, and it holds.

40
00:02:27,179 --> 00:02:30,835
A truck crosses it. A truck
too heavy brings it down.

41
00:02:30,915 --> 00:02:36,012
Both outcomes are real, and neither needs
the bridge to exist in its own right.

42
00:02:36,092 --> 00:02:38,756
Nor are the conditions
a hidden foundation.

43
00:02:38,836 --> 00:02:41,637
They are patterns too,
named in the same way.

44
00:02:41,717 --> 00:02:46,179
There is no bottom layer, only
the web and its vivid patterns.

45
00:02:47,033 --> 00:02:48,924
Fourth, karma and habit.

46
00:02:49,004 --> 00:02:53,013
What appears to each mind is shaped
by the tendencies it carries.

47
00:02:53,093 --> 00:02:55,531
People see water as something to drink.

48
00:02:55,634 --> 00:03:01,356
Fish see it as a home. In the old image,
hungry ghosts see it as pus and blood.

49
00:03:01,436 --> 00:03:04,005
Each version acts on the one who meets it.

50
00:03:04,085 --> 00:03:08,611
A rope in dim light is seen as
a snake, and the fear is real,

51
00:03:08,691 --> 00:03:10,663
though no snake was ever there.

52
00:03:10,743 --> 00:03:13,910
Habit is not a hidden
cause behind appearances.

53
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:16,904
It is how they come to
look solid and separate.

54
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:19,851
So two errors loosen together.

55
00:03:19,931 --> 00:03:23,370
Nothing stands behind appearances
holding them in place.

56
00:03:23,450 --> 00:03:26,595
And without such a ground,
they are not unreal.

57
00:03:27,406 --> 00:03:32,136
They are vivid, workable and
empty, with real consequences,

58
00:03:32,216 --> 00:03:36,556
and they can be met without the grasping
that made them seem like things.

